# Waveshare ESP32-P4-Module-DEV-KIT (and the -A / -B / -C kits, SKU 30560/30772/
# 30843/30844 - the letters only change which DSI screen is in the box)
#
# Build it with:
#   idf.py -B build.moduledevkit -D SDKCONFIG=build.moduledevkit/sdkconfig \
#     -D SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;boards/moduledevkit_p4.defaults" build
#
# Everything on this board that the KVM touches is an ESP32-P4-Module: a P4NRW32
# (32 MB PSRAM in package), an ESP32-C6 and 16 MB of flash under one shield. The
# carrier adds the RJ45, the card slot, the USB, the codec and a 2x20 header.
#
# Read off the published schematic (ESP32-P4-Module-DEV-KIT.pdf, files.waveshare.com),
# and it is the same layout as the boards already here:
#   Ethernet (IP101GRI): TX_EN 49, TXD0 34, TXD1 35, CRS_DV 28, RXD0 29, RXD1 30,
#                        MDC 31, MDIO 52, REF_CLK 50, PHY reset 51. PHY address 1
#                        (PHY_AD0 pulled up through 5.1K, PHY_AD3 down) - the
#                        firmware default.
#   microSD: CLK 43, CMD 44, D0 39, D1 40, D2 41, D3 42, and SD1_VDD through an
#            AO3401 P-channel MOSFET off GPIO 45, so active low.
#   ESP32-C6: inside the module. GPIO 14-19 are the only numbers the module does
#             not bring out to a pad, which is the SDIO link - the same six pins
#             as the Function EV board, so the same esp-hosted profile.
#   Capture I2C: SDA 7, SCL 8, with 2.2K pull-ups on the CSI connector.
#   BOOT button: GPIO 35, which is also Ethernet TXD1 - the sharing the password
#   reset already handles by reading the pin once at start-up.
#   Console: a CH343P on the Type-C, so UART on 37/38.
#
# The CSI connector is the 15-pin 1.0 mm one, wired to the Raspberry Pi camera
# standard: 2/3 D0-, 5/6 D1-, 8/9 CLK, 11/12 the two camera control lines, 13/14
# I2C SCL/SDA, 15 3V3, 1/4/7/10 ground. That is the pinout a Geekworm C790
# ribbon expects, so the flat cable in the C790 box plugs straight in.
#
# The USB is worth reading twice. The module's OTG-HS goes into an FSUSB42UMX
# mux: with the jumper on the "device" side (H3 2-3, which is also where the 47K
# pull-up leaves it) the P4 reaches ONE of the Type-A sockets directly, and that
# is the KVM's keyboard and mouse. The other position sends it into a CH334F hub
# and gives three host ports instead, which is not what this firmware wants.
# The socket is a Type-A FEMALE and its VBUS is driven by the board, so the lead
# to the target must be an A-to-A cable with the 5 V wire cut or absent -
# otherwise the board's 5 V rail and the target's meet.
#
# NOT YET VERIFIED ON HARDWARE. Configured from the schematic and published so
# owners can try it, the same way the NANO and Guition targets started.

# --- flash and partitions ---------------------------------------------------
# 16 MB on the module, not the 32 MB of the P4-ETH, so the shared 16 MB table.
CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHSIZE_16MB=y
CONFIG_PARTITION_TABLE_CUSTOM_FILENAME="partitions_16mb.csv"

# --- silicon revision -------------------------------------------------------
# Left at the base build's pre-3.0 setting, which is what every Waveshare P4
# board seen so far has carried (rev 1.3). No rev 3.x twin is published yet:
# nobody has reported a rev 3.x unit of this board, and each twin is another
# image to build and keep in step. If one turns up - the boot log says
# "Chip rev: v3.x" and this image will not start on it at all - the twin is the
# two lines the other boards' *_rev3.defaults carry:
# CONFIG_ESP32P4_SELECTS_REV_LESS_V3=n
# CONFIG_ESP32P4_REV_MIN_300=y

# --- updates ----------------------------------------------------------------
CONFIG_KVM_UPDATE_URL="https://espkvm.github.io/espkvm/firmware/p4-module-devkit/manifest.json"

# --- WiFi co-processor ------------------------------------------------------
# The C6 is inside the module on the Function EV board's SDIO pins, so the same
# esp-hosted configuration applies - including the guard against its eager
# constructor init, which otherwise races the microSD for the one SD host.
CONFIG_KVM_WIFI=y
CONFIG_ESP_HOSTED_P4_DEV_BOARD_FUNC_BOARD=y
CONFIG_SLAVE_IDF_TARGET_ESP32C6=y
CONFIG_ESP_HOSTED_CP_TARGET_ESP32C6=y
CONFIG_ESP_HOSTED_AUTO_CALL_INIT_BEFORE_APP_MAIN=n

# --- microSD ----------------------------------------------------------------
CONFIG_KVM_SD_PWR_GPIO=45

# --- capture reset ----------------------------------------------------------
# The base default drives GPIO 23 as the TC358743's RESETN, which is how the
# ESP32-P4-ETH is wired. Here the CSI connector's two camera control lines go
# nowhere but a pull-up (a 10K on CSI_IO0, CSI_IO1 not fitted), and 23 is an
# ordinary header pin. The C790 has its own power-on reset, so leave it alone.
CONFIG_KVM_TC358743_RST_GPIO=-1

# Which board this is: names it in the console and picks the expansion header
# the Pins tab draws.
CONFIG_KVM_BOARD_WAVESHARE_MODULE_DEVKIT=y
